## Integration Test Patterns by Technology

Each interface technology has its own test class that extends a shared base (e.g., `CreateOrderIntegrationTest`). The test creates a **dynamic route** in `@BeforeAll` that sends messages through the interface.

### Messaging Interface Test Pattern (Kafka, AMQP, JMS, RabbitMQ, MQTT, AWS SQS)

```java
@BeforeAll
void setupRoute() throws Exception {
    ModelCamelContext mcc = camelContext.getCamelContextExtension()
        .getContextPlugin(ModelCamelContext.class);

    // Create a test route that publishes to the interface's topic/queue
    RouteDefinition rd = new RouteDefinition("direct:testKafkaCreateOrder");
    rd.to("kafka:{{${serviceName}.northbound-createorder-topic}}-" +
          "${header.Content-Type}");
    mcc.addRouteDefinition(rd);
}

@ParameterizedTest
@MethodSource("provideFormats")
void test_CreateOrder_With_Format(String scenario, String format, String txId) {
    // Build exchange with test data
    Exchange exchange = ExchangeBuilder.anExchange(camelContext).build();
    exchange.getIn().setHeader("Content-Type", format);
    exchange.getIn().setBody(readResource("data/inttest/api/" + format + "/createorder/..."));

    // Send through the test route
    fluentProducerTemplate.to("direct:testKafkaCreateOrder").withExchange(exchange).send();

    // Wait for async processing then verify backends
    Awaitility.await().atMost(Duration.ofSeconds(30)).untilAsserted(() -> {
        // Verify WireMock, database counts, message queues, etc.
    });
}
```

| Interface | Test Route Target | Key Difference |
|---|---|---|
| MQTT | `paho-mqtt5:{{topic}}-{format}?...` | Requires byte[] payload |


